{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1476045-adventure-aeon-society-creation-story","id":1476045,"title":"[Adventure!] Aeon Society creation story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-08T07:12:45-08:00","id":1476045,"title":"[Adventure!] Aeon Society creation story","content":"I'm new to <b>Trinity Continuum </b>- and I want to make across era chronicle, from Aeon Society creation till Aeon Space era. I want to show with first story creation of Aeon Society by <b>Adventure!</b> story. Do you have any story ideas to start Adventure! in 1922-23 (?), just half a year after Hammersmith Incident and/or Aeon Society creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-08-2022, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T07:44:47-08:00","id":1476047,"title":"","content":"For the firt half year after Hamersmith Max is disappeared and Michael is looking for him, that could be a great first episode idea.<br /> <br /> Max reappear afer sometime telling he was in the future and was inspired to create Aeon Society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T08:27:47-08:00","id":1476048,"title":"","content":"WHERE Mercer first reapered? When he returned to 1922?<br /> <br /> I want to add some pulp elements, typical for games genere. Maybe some lost temple?<br /> <br /> Nazis are too early for 1920s, but maybe other canonical enemy could show?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T09:28:00-08:00","id":1476051,"title":"","content":"The Adventure manuscript goes over what happened with Max starting on page 294, which gives some cool ideas that will be useful for your campaign.<br /> <br /> In terms of where he returns, it just says that Michael Donighal was the anchor that he used to find his way back to his &quot;present&quot; so the where is wherever you want. It does not that Max was pretty messed up after he returned to the present, and Michael took care of him during that time.<br /> <br /> If you're setting things close to the Hammersmith Incident, you could spend some time dealing with the changes to the world and the rise of the Inspired while Max is gone to set the stage, then have Max reappear and recruit the characters for the Aeon Society.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'd really be wary of for a game like this is focusing too much on the big name characters like Max, Michael, and Sara and relegating the player characters to watching other people do cool things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T09:41:28-08:00","id":1476052,"title":"","content":"Page 137 of the Adventure Manuscript has some neat descriptions of special environments like alien worlds and dimensional rifts that might inspire some creativity around strange pulp things to encounter.<br /> <br /> The Strange Places section starting on page 75 also has some awesome plothooks. They reference events in 1930 but easy to bump things back an have your player characters be the ones to discover locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T12:19:28-08:00","id":1476057,"title":"","content":"You may also want to track down the Adventure 1e book. The 2e book reads very much like a sequel to the first edition. For the most part 2e doesn't contradict the setting materials as established in 1e. I think it is a fun read and a great companion to the new edition and might fill in some blanks for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T12:39:57-08:00","id":1476059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1476045-adventure-aeon-society-creation-story?p=1476051#post1476051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I'd really be wary of for a game like this is focusing too much on the big name characters like Max, Michael, and Sara and relegating the player characters to watching other people do cool things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, the founders of the Aeon Society suffered this fate. Want to know anything about them besides the \u201cbig three\u201d? Buy the first edition; because the TC:A! manuscript focuses exclusively on Max, Michael, and Sara. Not even \u201cprimarily\u201d; the others don't even get mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T14:13:59-08:00","id":1476063,"title":"","content":"While Hammersmith's estate was the epicenter of the global flood of Telluric energies, it was hardly the only place affected. If you want to set your campaign immediately after the event, you could have your players become Inspired elsewhere, then spend their first few adventures trying to figure things out themselves (while fighting whatever hostile fortean phenomenon were spawned at the same time). After they get some experience under their belts, you could either have them track down the Aeon Society, or have the society track them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T14:49:03-08:00","id":1476171,"title":"","content":"Or you could have characters form their own factions. Something I was dissatisfied with in the Trinity corebook was the base assumption that all Talents join up with a group. Why not start your own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T01:14:28-08:00","id":1476195,"title":"","content":"There is nothing stopping you from doing that.You can always buy a new Path in game to reflect joining a new group. That is if you want to make an organization after you guys have all started the adventuring.<br /> If you want to say that you began the game already as part of your own group, then there are rules to make your own Path.<br /> <br /> Pointing this out since you said you were dissatisfied with that...the devs already have that option covered for you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T10:11:27-08:00","id":1476215,"title":"","content":"If you want the players' group to help with the very beginnings of the Aeon Society during the Roaring 20s, one of the benefits of the exhaustive list of Aeon founders not appearing in the Adventure Manuscript is that your players' characters could be on that list. Make sure there's an element in their backstories, either individually or as a group that ties them to Mercer, Styles, or another of the named founder. <br /> <br /> At that point, you'd only have to decide whether they're :<br /> 1) out recruiting members (maybe extending invitations to join to Crackshot or Safari Jack and hijinxes ensue),<br /> 2) engaging in intrigue and political maneuvering to get Aeon's foot in the door when in comes to the halls of power (noir detective rather than just pulp),<br /> 3) investigating strange people, events or locales as Aeon starts realizing the full scope of the Hammersmith incident and its many unintended consequences (either detective-style or explorer-style). <br /> 4) taking on a big name bad guy, possibly before they made it big. Some of the Inspired big bads would still be getting their bearings, offering opportunities a games set in the 30s wouldn't have (Help take down the Ubiquitous Dragon in 1926, or learn about Imam Khwarazmi ibn Abi Tirmidhi's visions and help talk him off the ledge so he uses them for better ends that establish a Muslim Luddite murder-cult)<br /> 5) Getting involved with aliens (get poor Felicia Smith home, ideally without putting our whole dimension at risk, establish diplomatic ties with the mysterious bird people of the Northern Lights, find a portal through time and space in a mysterious crystal cave and ending up meeting pre-ascension Yarrans) <br /> 6) Maybe even going with a more Primoris approach : deciding that Aeon is ill-advised and/or ineffective and establishing their own allegiance.<br /> 7) All of the above<br /> <br /> And that's just at the top of my head. I'm sure others on the forum have plenty of ideas too, but which ideas suit your game best also depends on what your players would enjoy<br /> <br /> You may want to establish a special foe or plot point that ties the various eras together for your chronicle. (The only good example I can think of is the demon Kupala in Transylvania Chronicles for V:tM) Something that ties it all together that is specific to your chronicle. It could be they fight Jackson Harley and his evil plots throughout all 3 eras, or it could be a game-changing artefact that stirs up trouble whenever it pops up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T01:01:43-07:00","id":1476769,"title":"","content":"I read 1E <b>Adventure!</b> - <b>Tales of the Aeon Society Rulebook </b>to get better view of Aeon start era...<br /> <br /> So... <b>Hammersmith Incident took place in manor in South London in July of 1922</b>. <b>Aeon Society is formed officially in June of 1923 in Chicago</b>, few months after Mencer return to present timeline. If going with 'find Max Mercer' first story, he needs to reaper somewhere in late 1922. Most logical would be that he reapers on the ruins of Hammersmith Manor in winter of 1922, on the snow falling from the sky... \ud83e\udd14 Maybe Christmas Day? To make it more melodramatic? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: I read in <b>Tales of the Aeon Society </b>that in January 1923, Donighal telegraph to Styles from Far East there are no clues about Mercer. And that Mercer show ups in Chicago in coming few weeks, two months tops.<br /> <br /> Now, having fixed great ending scene - we need proper plot of story to run. Michael Donighal is looking for Mencer for last year. As Dr. Primoris is all about (future Nova-like) powers over energies, he does not have good detective skills. He orders PCs to look for clues over his missing loved one. But then story becomes 'we need to look for last few days of Mercer on Earth'...<br /> <br /> <b>Need some 'false clue' or 'big twist' to send PCs to other part of the world</b> - and THEN return with knowledge to know that Mercer WILL be on Christmas Day of 1922 on ruins of Hammersmith... \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Some clue about time-travels - that imply that Mercer will return to the same place, later on. Maybe a 'secret Tibetan techniques'? As Donighal was looking in Far East, earlier on? Maybe add brand new Nazis then, maybe Tibet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-17-2022, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T03:15:41-07:00","id":1476773,"title":"","content":"Are there canonical images of Max Mercer and Michael Donighal in that 1920s era? Will probably need those for game running reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T08:35:41-07:00","id":1477630,"title":"","content":"Some research in this times, for the story. Seems like good antagonist in 1922-23 could be disillusioned Thule Occultist \u2013 that may or may not be Nazis sympathizer \u2013 looking for some \u2018occult knowledge\u2019 ( alien tech? ) in some faraway place\u2026 Asia maybe? Tibet, as occultist where entrenched in it? Some \u2018future sight\u2019 technique/technology by \u2018Tellurian Energies\u2019 \u2013 to players, in the end, predict Max will show up in Chicago?<br /> ( All quotes are from Wikipedia articles on main subject )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Thule Society</b></span><br /> <br /> The Thule Society was originally a &quot;German study group&quot; headed by Walter Nauhaus, a wounded World War I veteran turned art student from Berlin who had become a keeper of pedigrees for the Germanenorden (or &quot;Order of Teutons&quot;), a secret society founded in 1911 and formally named in the following year. In 1917, Nauhaus moved to Munich; his <i>Thule Society</i> was to be a cover-name for the Munich branch of the Germanenorden, but events developed differently as a result of a schism in the Order. In 1918, Nauhaus was contacted in Munich by Rudolf von Sebottendorf (or von Sebottendorff), an occultist and newly elected head of the Bavarian province of the schismatic offshoot known as the Germanenorden Walvater of the Holy Grail. The two men became associates in a recruitment campaign, and Sebottendorff adopted Nauhaus's Thule Society as a cover-name for his Munich lodge of the Germanenorden Walvater at its formal dedication on 18 August 1918.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nazis road to power</b></span><br /> <br /> (German Worker\u2019s Party) manifesto was antisemitic, anti-capitalist, anti-democratic, anti-Marxist and anti-liberal. To increase its appeal to larger segments of the population, on the same day as Hitler's <i>Hofbr\u00e4uhaus</i> speech on 24 February 1920, the DAP changed its name to the <i>Nationalsozialistische Deutsche Arbeiterpartei</i> (&quot;National Socialist German Workers' Party&quot;, or Nazi Party). The word &quot;Socialist&quot; was added by the party's executive committee, over Hitler's objections, in order to help appeal to left-wing workers.<br /> <br /> In 1920, the Nazi Party officially announced that only persons of &quot;pure Aryan descent [<i>rein arischer Abkunft</i>]&quot; could become party members and if the person had a spouse, the spouse also had to be a &quot;racially pure&quot; Aryan. Party members could not be related either directly or indirectly to a so-called &quot;non-Aryan&quot;. Even before it had become legally forbidden by the Nuremberg Laws in 1935, the Nazis banned sexual relations and marriages between party members and Jews. Party members found guilty of <i>Rassenschande</i> (&quot;racial defilement&quot;) were persecuted heavily. Some members were even sentenced to death.<br /> <br /> Hitler quickly became the party's most active orator, appearing in public as a speaker 31 times within the first year after his self-discovery. Crowds began to flock to hear his speeches. Hitler always spoke about the same subjects: the Treaty of Versailles and the Jewish question. This deliberate technique and effective publicising of the party contributed significantly to his early success, about which a contemporary poster wrote: &quot;Since Herr Hitler is a brilliant speaker, we can hold out the prospect of an extremely exciting evening.&quot;<br /> <br /> Over the following months, the party continued to attract new members, while remaining too small to have any real significance in German politics. By the end of the year, party membership was recorded at 2,000 - many of whom Hitler and R\u00f6hm had brought into the party personally, or for whom Hitler's oratory had been their reason for joining.<br /> <br /> Hitler's talent as an orator and his ability to draw new members, combined with his characteristic ruthlessness, soon made him the dominant figure. However, while Hitler and Eckart were on a fundraising trip to Berlin in June 1921, a mutiny broke out within the party in Munich. Members of its executive committee wanted to merge with the rival German Socialist Party (DSP). Upon returning to Munich on 11 July, Hitler angrily tendered his resignation. The committee members realised that his resignation would mean the end of the party. Hitler announced he would rejoin on condition that he would replace Drexler as party chairman, and that the party headquarters would remain in Munich.The committee agreed, and he rejoined the party on 26 July as member 3,680. Hitler continued to face some opposition within the NSDAP, as his opponents had Hermann Esser expelled from the party and they printed 3,000 copies of a pamphlet attacking Hitler as a traitor to the party. In the following days, Hitler spoke to several packed houses and defended himself and Esser to thunderous applause.<br /> His strategy proved successful; at a special party congress on 29 July 1921, he replaced Drexler as party chairman by a vote of 533 to 1. The committee was dissolved, and Hitler was granted nearly absolute powers as the party's sole leader. He would hold the post for the remainder of his life. Hitler soon acquired the title <i>F\u00fchrer</i> (&quot;leader&quot;) and after a series of sharp internal conflicts it was accepted that the party would be governed by the <i>F\u00fchrerprinzip</i> (&quot;leader principle&quot;). Under this principle, the party was a highly centralised entity that functioned strictly from the top down, with Hitler at the apex as the party's absolute leader. Hitler saw the party as a revolutionary organisation, whose aim was the overthrow of the Weimar Republic, which he saw as controlled by the socialists, Jews and the &quot;November criminals&quot; who had betrayed the German soldiers in 1918. The SA (&quot;storm troopers&quot;, also known as &quot;Brownshirts&quot;) were founded as a party militia in 1921 and began violent attacks on other parties.<br /> <br /> For Hitler, the twin goals of the party were always German nationalist expansionism and antisemitism. These two goals were fused in his mind by his belief that Germany's external enemies\u2014Britain, France and the Soviet Union\u2014were controlled by the Jews and that Germany's future wars of national expansion would necessarily entail a war of annihilation against them. For Hitler and his principal lieutenants, national and racial issues were always dominant. This was symbolised by the adoption as the party emblem of the swastika. In German nationalist circles, the swastika was considered a symbol of an &quot;Aryan race&quot; and it symbolised the replacement of the Christian Cross with allegiance to a National Socialist State.<br /> <br /> The Nazi Party grew significantly during 1921 and 1922, partly through Hitler's oratorical skills, partly through the SA's appeal to unemployed young men, and partly because there was a backlash against socialist and liberal politics in Bavaria as Germany's economic problems deepened and the weakness of the Weimar regime became apparent. The party recruited former World War I soldiers, to whom Hitler as a decorated frontline veteran could particularly appeal, as well as small businessmen and disaffected former members of rival parties. Nazi rallies were often held in beer halls, where downtrodden men could get free beer. The Hitler Youth was formed for the children of party members. The party also formed groups in other parts of Germany. Julius Streicher in Nuremberg was an early recruit and became editor of the racist magazine <i>Der St\u00fcrmer</i>. In December 1920, the Nazi Party had acquired a newspaper, the <i>V\u00f6lkischer Beobachter</i>, of which its leading ideologist Alfred Rosenberg became editor. Others to join the party around this time were Heinrich Himmler and World War I flying ace Hermann G\u00f6ring.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Adoption of Italian fascism: The Beer Hall Putsch</b></span><br /> On 31 October 1922, a fascist party with similar policies and objectives came into power in Italy, the National Fascist Party, under the leadership of the charismatic Benito Mussolini. The Fascists, like the Nazis, promoted a national rebirth of their country, as they opposed communism and liberalism; appealed to the working-class; opposed the Treaty of Versailles; and advocated the territorial expansion of their country. Hitler was inspired by Mussolini and the Fascists, beginning to adopt elements of the Fascist's and Mussolini for the Nazi Party and himself. The Italian Fascists also used a straight-armed Roman salute and wore black-shirted uniforms; Hitler would later borrow their use of the straight-armed salute as a Nazi salute.<br /> <br /> When the Fascists took control of Italy through their coup d'\u00e9tat called the &quot;March on Rome&quot;, Hitler began planning his own coup less than a month later In January 1923, France occupied the Ruhr industrial region as a result of Germany's failure to meet its reparations payments. This led to economic chaos, the resignation of Wilhelm Cuno's government and an attempt by the German Communist Party (KPD) to stage a revolution. The reaction to these events was an upsurge of nationalist sentiment. Nazi Party membership grew sharply to about 20,000. By November 1923, Hitler had decided that the time was right for an attempt to seize power in Munich, in the hope that the <i>Reichswehr</i> (the post-war German military) would mutiny against the Berlin government and join his revolt. In this, he was influenced by former General Erich Ludendorff, who had become a supporter\u2014though not a member\u2014of the Nazis\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-23-2022, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T11:31:22-07:00","id":1477637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1476045-adventure-aeon-society-creation-story?p=1476773#post1476773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there canonical images of Max Mercer and Michael Donighal in that 1920s era? Will probably need those for game running reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you have the TC: Aeon core, there's a 1920s-era picture of them, along with other big-name members, on p. 357 (reproduced from the original run). Max is the one in the middle, and Michael is the one second from left with the dark glasses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T21:48:33-07:00","id":1478999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1476045-adventure-aeon-society-creation-story?p=1476769#post1476769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I read in <b>Tales of the Aeon Society </b>that in January 1923, Donighal telegraph to Styles from Far East there are no clues about Mercer. And that Mercer show ups in Chicago in coming few weeks, two months tops.<br /> (...)<br /> Some clue about time-travels - that imply that Mercer will return to the same place, later on. Maybe a 'secret Tibetan techniques'? As Donighal was looking in Far East, earlier on? Maybe add brand new Nazis then, maybe Tibet?</div> </div> </div> </div>SO I'm more and more firm in the story - pices are falling in to places. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I now have antagonist of the tale - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1478161-character-creation-for-tc-2e#post1478161\"><b>Ferdinand 'Franz' Herz</b></a> - in early 1923, Thule occultists, now Mesmerits, plagued by the nightmares about something called 'AEON', showing in his head... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Franz is telepath and <a href=\"https://psychonauts.fandom.com/wiki/Astral_Projection\" target=\"_blank\">'psychonaut'</a> ( abilities, not gov agent ) , but he wanted to dwell more - into FUTURE, to see future in his mind. He travel to Tibet to learn those Future Sight techniques, where he cross paths with PCs on Michael Donighal investigation.<br /> <br /> <b>Now how to connect Franz quest for Future Sight with Donighal investigation for Mercer?</b> \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T02:25:28-07:00","id":1479226,"title":"","content":"Possible twist - <b>Maybe <i>i</i><i>t's Max</i> that is looking for Future Sight?</b> After being sent to to future at Hammersmith, he returned - but still want's to see future of the World. It would make logical then that he travels a lot, finally showing in Tibet. Micheal then hire PCs to find Max that was shown in few photos around the world - last in Tibet...<br /> <br /> With Franz being natural competition, looking for the same Gift in Tibet - and we then have story 2nd Act - race for Future Sight Temple! \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-23-2022, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T22:38:53-07:00","id":1487546,"title":"","content":"Past 3 months, got some better grasp on the material and few events came to be. First, there was world premier of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f_vbAtFSEc0\" target=\"_blank\"><b>RRR (Rise Roar Revolt) 2022</b></a> - Teluga ( south India ) made nationalistic, over the top action drama, set in British Raj in 1920s were heroes are opposing cruel Empire rule. You just <u><b>need</b></u> to see it - it's 'Indian Hollywood' as it bet, totally different take on blockbusters!<br /> <br /> Second is that in <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aether-tabletop-roleplaying-game\" target=\"_blank\"><b>TC Aether</b>, now on Kickstarter</a>, there are background information about Inspired-like Aether users BEFORE 1920-30s <b>Adventure!</b> era. It's great fountain for new Trinity Continuum background information, new takes on Telluric energies - and has Mina Harker and Nicola Tesla as heroes! Go on, and back it till it is - you will not regret it!<br /> <br /> <b>TC Aether</b> has also India region<b> <i>Three Prongs</i></b> Society that by 1880s have been using <i><b>Shakti</b></i> - their term on Aether and Telluric - for centuries, as monastic order dedicated to Kali. Adding that for Aether 1890s era is used Martian invasion as plot point, we have British Army special division ( <b><i>HRH-PDP</i></b> ) to fight aliens, using Aether. Cool would be to used them also in the background - but I have a bit problem to rename British division. Will explore it in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1487143-trinity-timeline-aether-happened-but-no-martian-invasion\">alternative timeline topic for the Aether era</a>.<br /> <br /> In the end, story will be still about looking for Max Mercer and race for Future Sight against 'Franz' Thulist - only set in British Raj of 1923, with possible involvement of Three Prongs and HRH-PDP (under different name ). But it will end in creation of Aeon Society as we know it. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> As I wanted to put Future Sight race in deep mountains, I think about locating story in Katmandu, in Nepal, on Indian-Chinese border. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-23-2022, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T20:00:47-07:00","id":1492850,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Relic - <i>Future Sight Urn</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VZ3WgsN.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}